# Line endings, stated once instead of inferred per machine.
#
# The repository stores LF. Without this file, a Windows checkout with the common
# core.autocrlf=true setting rewrites every file to CRLF in the working tree, which made
# `eslint` report thousands of linebreak-style errors locally while the same code passed on Linux
# CI. The rule is now off in .eslintrc.json and this file keeps checkouts consistent instead.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only helpers keep CRLF, because PowerShell's own tooling is happier with it.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binaries: never touched.
*.pem binary
*.der binary
*.keystore binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.apk binary
